# NoteHub API

A backend REST API for a note-taking application built with Node.js and Express.

## Features

- User authentication (register, login, logout)
- JWT-based authorization with refresh tokens
- Password reset via email
- CRUD operations for notes
- Protected routes for authenticated users
- Avatar upload support
- Request validation using Joi + celebrate middleware

## Tech Stack

- Node.js
- Express.js
- MongoDB
- JWT Authentication
- Multer (file uploads)
- Nodemailer (email service)
- Celebrate / Joi (validation)

## Auth Routes

- `POST /auth/register` – register new user
- `POST /auth/login` – user login
- `POST /auth/logout` – logout user
- `POST /auth/refresh` – refresh session
- `POST /auth/request-reset-email` – request password reset email
- `POST /auth/reset-password` – reset password

## Notes Routes (protected)

- `GET /notes` – get all notes
- `GET /notes/:noteId` – get note by ID
- `POST /notes` – create new note
- `DELETE /notes/:noteId` – delete note
- `PATCH /notes/:noteId` – update note

## User Routes

- `PATCH /users/me/avatar` – update user avatar (file upload)

## Authentication

Most routes require JWT authentication via middleware.

## Installation

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```
